+# Daily Grind security audit
+
+## Findings and changes
+
+| Area | Finding | Implemented protection |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Logout | The old endpoint only printed a message. | The navigation submits a native POST form. POST `/logout` expires received cookie names at `Path=/` and returns `Clear-Site-Data` for cookies, storage, cache, prefetch cache, and prerender cache. GET/HEAD show a confirmation without changing state. |
+| Cross-origin requests | A logout link can be followed by crawlers, speculative navigation, or another site. | State changes require POST; Fetch Metadata and Origin checks reject cross-origin submissions. No redirect target is accepted. |
+| HTML | An inline stylesheet and an inline style attribute would break a restrictive style policy. | All styling is in `/styles.css`; no inline styles, event handlers, executable URLs, or scripts remain. The existing coffee image and page layout are preserved. |
+| Client scripts | There are no client-side scripts, dependencies, DOM injection sinks, dynamic HTML, or third-party script tags. | CSP disables all scripts, workers, connections, frames, and other resources by default. Trusted Types enforcement rejects string-based script injection sinks and creation of new policies in supporting browsers. No permissive default policy is created. |
+| Resource policy | No security headers were present. | CSP permits only local styles and local/Unsplash images. It forbids embedding, plugins, base URL overrides, and off-origin form submission. Every application response, including errors and assets, receives security headers. |
+| Browser data | Responses could be retained by intermediary and HTTP browser caches. | All responses use `Cache-Control: no-store`; logout also explicitly requests browser data removal. |
+| Additional headers | MIME sniffing, referrer disclosure, framing, opener access, and device capabilities had no restrictions. | `nosniff`, `no-referrer`, `DENY`, same-origin opener/resource policies, and a restrictive Permissions Policy are set. |
+| File serving | Every path previously returned the homepage. | Only named public assets and existing navigation routes are served. Unknown paths return 404, unsupported methods return 405, HEAD omits bodies, and repository files are inaccessible through the handler. |
+
+## Deployment
+
+- `npm start` runs the dependency-free Node server. The default port remains `11222`; set `PORT` to override it.
+- Serve production traffic over HTTPS at a reverse proxy. Set `PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://your-domain.example` to the exact browser-visible origin, including a nonstandard port if applicable. This configures logout Origin validation behind the proxy and enables HSTS with a one-year lifetime. HTTP deployments omit HSTS. Forwarded protocol headers are deliberately not trusted. Do not enable this HTTPS configuration for a domain until TLS is ready.
+- Preserve the application's response headers at the proxy. Avoid adding a conflicting CSP. Keep the existing `https://images.unsplash.com` image source permitted; no cross-origin embedder policy is added that would break it.
+- The enforced CSP matches the audited, script-free markup. When adding new resources or scripts, audit their required origins and DOM operations first. Trial proposed changes with `Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only` in staging and a controlled report collector before changing the enforced policy; do not add `unsafe-inline`, `unsafe-eval`, wildcard sources, or a permissive Trusted Types policy to mask failures. No public report receiver is exposed by this server.
+
+## Limits and validation
+
+This repository has no login flow, identity provider, tokens, or server-side session store. Logout clears browser state; if authentication is introduced, revoke the server-side session or refresh token before returning success. Cookie expiration only covers received cookies with root path and host scope. `Clear-Site-Data` handles broader browser cleanup on supporting secure contexts, but cookie clearing can also affect sibling subdomains. Use a dedicated site for this deployment. Older browsers may ignore some directives; cache-control and cookie expiration remain independent protections. Browser history and already-open documents are not guaranteed to be erased.
+
+`npm run build` performs syntax checks without starting a server or importing its entrypoint. Static review covers the markup, CSS resource origins, response headers, routing, and logout flow. No browser or live HTTP verification was performed, as requested; runtime behavior and browser compatibility have not been exercised.
+
+References: [Clear-Site-Data and secure contexts](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Clear-Site-Data), [CSP](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Guides/CSP), and [Trusted Types enforcement](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Content-Security-Policy/require-trusted-types-for).
